  "behavior": [
    "Naturally aligned scalar atomics and compare-exchange preserve old values, success flags and live inputs.",
    "Private pointer and boolean flow preserves significant bits, symbols and two-word layouts. The confirmed dirty-upper-bit boolean branch regression is fixed.",
    "Bounded frame addresses and scaled indexes preserve byte offsets, and reachable CFG scheduling respects definitions without dropping unreachable blocks.",
    "Direct C integer/pointer variadic calls use existing register and stack ownership through sixteen arguments. Only ordinary known function symbols and exact advisory pointer contracts are admitted.",
    "Full-width accumulator aliases survive immediate operations and later spills; poisoned-spill tests reproduce the old stale upper half and prove the repair.",
    "The unchanged pinned upstream Fibonacci program executes all six assertions in ReleaseFast and ReleaseSmall with LLVM-equivalent exit status, stdout and stderr."
  ],
  "known_boundaries": [
    "The separately diagnosed narrow arithmetic-shift error remains in this accepted checkpoint. Its tested repair is in the integer prototype and awaits the next cumulative full integration.",
    "ReleaseSafe whole-program emission remains incomplete: 1478 of 1568 functions emit and 90 fail; no Safe local object or execution is claimed.",
    "The authorized plan continues through remaining scalar, memory, vector, CFG and ABI forms, pinned runtime linkage, and unchanged ReleaseSafe execution with a mandatory permanent three-mode regression."
  ],
